.TH BATTERY 1
.SH NAME
battery \- battery, AC and lid
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B battery
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B battery
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It asks the ACPI server,
.BR acpid (4),
and prints on one line: the battery's charge in percent, whether it is
charging, not charging or discharging, the time to full or left, its
charge now, when full and by design (mWh or mAh), the rate and the
voltage; then whether AC power is on, whether the lid is open or closed,
and how many times the machine woke from sleep.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 when there is no ACPI server (not a PC, or not a laptop).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acpid (4),
.BR poweroff (8)
